spanned by the vectors. Computing the images of ${i,j}$ under $A$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =Ai=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j \\\\ {j}^{′} & =Aj=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/77936c4115b37d79ae301a93b218ecd23114ae4ad42d8298b8f058c1f50e82a2.png)\n\nSo, the matrix represents a rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians **clockwise** about the origin.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ **clockwise** by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/e941207a92a2b688428c55be3bc17856ea47fa2e11db8e3dc571b88ebbe8e3b1.png)" 13194139534395 true] [17592186286124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286125 13194139534395 true] [17592186286124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286126 13194139534395 true] [17592186286124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286127 13194139534395 true] [17592186286124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286128 13194139534395 true] [17592186286124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286129 13194139534395 true] [17592186286124 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534395 true] [17592186286124 1041 "selection" 13194139534395 true] [17592186286124 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286128 13194139534395 true] [17592186286124 1110 #uuid "e433f5d2-bb77-5783-a60a-e5781b101597" 13194139534395 true] [17592186286125 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/e3fe0bfa8161108c3d5edc48a6df4a52fe2c5b4dbf1c9964cf82e4f257ff357c.png" 13194139534395 true] [17592186286125 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534395 true] [17592186286125 1111 #uuid "bf3c118a-93f1-5a86-bf30-b0f